{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ונבקה.</b> From the root of בוקק (Isaiah 24:1), like the meaning מריק, and ונבקה is in the nif'al pattern from doubled-root verbs, like ונסבה ורחבה (Ezekiel 41:7):" "<b>האטים.</b> From the root of ויהלך אט (1 Kings 21:27) — the deeds that are done in secret:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:13.371479840Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}